"I need you to build a strategy deck storyline for the following situation.\n\nAudience: Series B investor meeting (lead VC partner + two associates)\nDecision: whether to lead a $45M Series B in Fieldlark, a B2B SaaS platform for agricultural supply chain compliance.\n\n---\n**FIELDLARK — SERIES B DATA PACKAGE (compiled by CFO, Nov 2026)**\n\n| Metric | Value | Note |\n|---|---|---||\n| ARR (Oct 31, 2026) | $8.2M | Contracted annual value of active subscriptions |\n| Bookings (FY2026, fiscal year ending Sep 30) | $11.4M | Includes multi-year contract TCV recognized at signing |\n| YoY ARR growth | 61% | Oct 2025 ARR was $5.1M |\n| Net Revenue Retention | 118% | Trailing 12 months |\n| Gross Margin | 71% | Trailing 12 months |\n| CAC Payback | 19 months | Based on new logo ARR / fully-loaded sales & marketing spend |\n| Logo churn | 2.1% | Annual, trailing 12 months |\n| Headcount | 47 | Full-time employees |\n| Total Addressable Market | $3.4B | Third-party estimate, North American ag-compliance software |\n| Series A raised | $12M | Closed March 2024 |\n\nNote A: The FY2026 bookings figure ($11.4M) includes a $3.1M multi-year enterprise deal with Greyhorn Cooperative signed in August. This deal has an unusually long implementation period (18 months) and revenue recognition begins in Q2 2027. It is not yet reflected in ARR.\n\nNote B: The 61% YoY ARR growth rate compares October 2025 to October 2026. The company's fiscal year ends September 30, so the two figures straddle two fiscal years. The company separately reports FY2026 ARR growth (fiscal year basis) as 44% — from $4.3M to $6.2M — a figure that excludes the strong Q4 calendar 2026 bookings cohort.\n\nNote C: ARR as of October 31 ($8.2M) is a point-in-time snapshot; the sales team has indicated three additional enterprise deals (~$1.9M combined ARR) are in final negotiation, expected to close by December 31. These are not in the ARR figure.\n\nNote D: CAC Payback of 19 months is calculated on new logo ARR. If calculated on new logo ARR net of first-year implementation and onboarding costs (which average $18K per new logo), payback extends to approximately 26 months.\n\n---\nPlease produce the full four-artifact storyline plus self-check."